# Containment Protocol — Cursor plugin keep-list

Canonical detail: **`docs/agent-cursor-plugins.md`**.

## Use

- **Linear** — mandatory issue lifecycle (see `linear-always-update.mdc`). After an implementation PR merges, Cloud Agents that cannot auth Linear emit a local-agent handoff (`cloud-agent-linear-handoff.mdc`).
- **Tavily** — live web research only after repo sources; never into game runtime/CI.
- **Sonatype** — **required** before adding/upgrading npm deps (`/check-dependency` or MCP). Guide Agent P CI: `.github/workflows/agp-workflow.yml` (OIDC; do not commit Guide tokens or `agp.yml`).
- **Snyk** — optional on-demand SCA/SAST/package health; does not replace Sonatype; no parallel Snyk CI gates without a Linear slice.
- **Modern Web Guidance** — when installed, search before inventing HTML/CSS/client-JS UI patterns; still obey layer boundaries and existing design system.
- **Figma** — UI visual bridge only; CSS (`src/index.css`) is shipped token source of truth; use `docs/figma-integration.md` + `docs/figma/*` + skill `cp-figma-ui-bridge`; never wire Figma SDK into `src/` or CI for this bridge.
- **Figma subscription / auth blocker (mandatory):** When the active task needs a Figma capability (edit the canonical UI System file, design→code from a Figma frame, sync tokens/components in Figma) and a missing/lapsed Figma subscription, plan tier, or MCP auth blocks that capability — **stop and prompt the human** to subscribe, renew, upgrade, or complete auth. Do **not** silently skip Figma or substitute a weaker path without telling them. Do **not** prompt when the slice does not need Figma (domain/sim, or UI solvable from existing React/CSS alone).
- **Google Drive** — collaborative drafts bridge (story/social/design); repo remains SoT for shipped code; use `docs/google-drive-integration.md` + `docs/google-drive/*` + skill `cp-google-drive-bridge`; never wire Drive SDK into `src/` or CI; new writes under agent-owned registry folders (`drive.file`).
- **Google Drive auth blocker (mandatory):** When the active task needs Drive and MCP auth / Google account access blocks it — **stop and prompt the human** to connect or re-auth. Do **not** silently skip. Do **not** prompt when the slice does not need Drive.
- **PR reviewers** — enforce via `.coderabbit.yaml`, `.greptile/`, `.amazonq/rules/`, `AGENTS.md` Review guidelines.

## Do not

- Wire search, scan, or SaaS SDKs into `src/` or CI unless the active Linear slice requires it.
- Treat marketplace plugins as installable from the agent — human installs; agent documents and uses.
- Expand scope to enterprise DB/ops/auth/sales plugins for this client-only SPA.
- Silently skip a needed Figma step because the human has no active subscription — prompt first.
- Silently skip a needed Google Drive step because MCP auth failed — prompt first.
